Top Interview Questions
What is the role of API Server?

Single entry point to the cluster.

Why etcd is important?

Stores entire cluster state.

What happens when Scheduler fails?

Running Pods continue; new Pods stay Pending.

What does Kubelet do?

Manages Pods on a node.

Difference between Kubelet and Kube-Proxy?
Plain Text
Kubelet -> Pod lifecycle
KubeProxy -> Service networking
How does Kubernetes maintain desired state?

Using controllers in Controller Manager.

In EKS, who provisions a LoadBalancer?

Cloud Controller Manager communicates with AWS APIs.

Where does Karpenter fit?

For your EKS interviews:

Plain Text
Pending Pod
|
Karpenter watches
|
Creates EC2 Instance
|
Node Joins Cluster
|
Scheduler places Pod

Since you've recently worked on Cluster Autoscaler and Karpenter, interviewers often ask:

Plain Text
Scheduler decides WHERE a pod runs.
Karpenter decides WHEN to create a new node.

This single line is a strong senior-level answer.

